,"startLine":201,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":215,"endLineOffset":9,"length":664},{"pos":9184,"endPos":9189,"startLine":217,"startLineOffset":12,"endLine":217,"endLineOffset":17,"length":6},{"pos":9555,"endPos":9560,"startLine":223,"startLineOffset":38,"endLine":223,"endLineOffset":43,"length":6}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":8459,"endPos":8477,"startLine":199,"startLineOffset":23,"endLine":199,"endLineOffset":41,"length":19},{"pos":8480,"endPos":8534,"startLine":199,"startLineOffset":44,"endLine":199,"endLineOffset":98,"length":55},{"pos":8544,"endPos":8717,"startLine":200,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":202,"endLineOffset":9,"length":174},{"pos":8727,"endPos":8808,"startLine":204,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":204,"endLineOffset":89,"length":82},{"pos":8821,"endPos":8840,"startLine":205,"startLineOffset":12,"endLine":205,"endLineOffset":31,"length":20},{"pos":9207,"endPos":9253,"startLine":212,"startLineOffset":38,"endLine":212,"endLineOffset":84,"length":47}]}]}],"groundTruthGeneratedCommentsNodes":[{"groundTruth":{"original_line":956,"line":955,"comment_lines":["[][955]"],"review_comment":["This `isDataStreamTimestampFieldEnabled` check is unfortunate. The reason for it being here is that we can\u0027t fully trust `MapperBuilderContext#isDataStream`. In its current implementation `isDataStream` starts as `false` and then gets flipped to `true` if `DataStreamTimestampFieldMapper` is enabled in **current** mapping. This is broken for an edge case of a mapping overriding default `@timestamp` mapping (it is more generally broken for any mapping updates but this is the first time we experience that).\r\n\r\nScenario:\r\n1. Create a time series index with default mapping only\r\n2. Update mapping with\r\n```\r\n{\"@timestamp\": {\"type\": \"date\"}}\r\n```\r\nFor this mapping update `isDataStream` is `false` even though it was `true` previously.\r\n\r\nOne option to fix this is to pass existing mapping into `MappingParser#parse` and initialize `isDataStream` to a value based on it. I didn\u0027t want to mix this change in here.","Thanks for this explanation. Let\u0027s make fixing `MapperBuilderContext#isDataStream()` a followup of this change. As part of that change the ` \u0026\u0026 context.mappingLookup().isDataStreamTimestampFieldEnabled()` part of the condition can be removed."],"path":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DateFieldMapper.java","id":36737,"created_at":"2024-07-08T21:33:57Z","original_position":55,"side":"RIGHT","position":47,"submitted_on_commit":"f51dd2cd5350241e08accfe888e0c06d72861868","diff_hunk":"@@ -942,6 +947,30 @@ protected void parseCreateField(DocumentParserContext context) throws IOExceptio\n     }\n \n     private void indexValue(DocumentParserContext context, long timestamp) {\n+        // DataStreamTimestampFieldMapper and TsidExtractingFieldMapper need to use timestamp value,\n+        // so when this is true we store it in a well-known place\n+        // instead of forcing them to iterate over all fields.\n+        //\n+        // DataStreamTimestampFieldMapper is present and enabled both\n+        // in data streams and standalone indices in time_series mode\n+        if (isDataStreamTimestampField \u0026\u0026 context.mappingLookup().isDataStreamTimestampFieldEnabled()) {","submitted_line":956},"generatedCommentsNodes":[]}],"coveredGroundTruth":0,"uncoveredGroundTruth":1,"coveredMatchable":4,"uncoveredMatchable":11,"timing":17210,"tokensIn":6978,"tokensOut":578}